/Producer (PyPDF2)
/Title (Proca\040Metamaterials\054\040Massive\040Electromagnetism\054\040and\040Nonlocality)
/Author (Said\040Mikki)
/Subject (We\040investigate\040a\040new\040type\040of\040electromagnetic\040meta\055materials\040\050MTMs\051\054\040which\040we\040dub\040Proca\040MTMs\054\040constituting\040an\040interesting\040medium\040behaving\040like\040a\040\215relativistic\040material\216\040for\040potential\040use\040in\040electromagnetic\040applications\056\040It\040is\040rigorously\040proved\040using\040a\040field\055theoretic\040approach\040that\040Maxwell\040theory\040inside\040certain\040classes\040of\040nonlocal\040metamaterials\040is\040equivalent\040to\040Maxwell\055Proca\040theory\040in\040vacuum\054\040where\040in\040the\040latter\040photons\040acquire\040a\040nonzero\040mass\040\050massive\040electromagnetism\056\051\040It\040turns\040out\040that\040the\040key\040to\040the\040operation\040of\040Proca\040MTM\040is\040nonlocality\040\050here\040spatial\040dispersion\040since\040the\040Proca\040MTM\040is\040homogeneous\051\054\040and\040hence\040Proca\040MTMs\040represent\040an\040important\040example\040of\040the\040more\040general\040family\040of\040nonlocal\040MTMs\056\040Our\040analysis\040involves\040multiphysics\040aspects\054\040utilizing\040concepts\040and\040methods\040taken\040from\040classical\040electromagnetism\054\040special\040relativity\054\040quantum\040theory\054\040electromagnetic\040materials\054\040and\040antenna\040theory\056\040Extensive\040discussion\040of\040the\040physics\054\040computational\040methods\054\040and\040design\040parameters\040of\040Proca\040MTMs\040is\040provided\040to\040further\040understand\040the\040nature\040of\040massive\040electromagnetism\040in\040nonlocal\040MTMs\056\040Proca\040waves\040carry\040an\040additional\040polarization\040degree\040of\040freedom\040and\040each\040wave\040appears\040to\040behave\040like\040a\040single\040mode\040with\040two\040transverse\040components\040and\040one\040longitudinal\056\040This\040opens\040the\040door\040for\040applications\040in\040wireless\040communications\040and\040other\040fields\040where\040information\040could\040be\040encoded\040in\040polarization\056\040As\040a\040concrete\040application\054\040we\040develop\040the\040main\040ingredients\040of\040Proca\040antennas\040as\040an\040example\040of\040the\040emerging\040technology\040of\040nonlocal\040antennas\054\040where\040we\040establish\040that\040a\040single\040Proca\040dipole\040possesses\040a\040perfect\040isotropic\040radiation\040pattern\054\040a\040radical\040departure\040from\040conventional\040local\040antennas\040\050radiators\040in\040vacuum\040and\040temporally\040dispersive\040media\051\040where\040such\040radiation\040characteristics\040is\040impossible\056\040Moreover\054\040the\040new\040connection\040between\040electromagnetic\040theory\040in\040some\040nonlocal\040MTMs\040and\040Maxwell\055Proca\040theory\040allows\040the\040use\040of\040relativistic\040techniques\040developed\040in\040the\040latter\040in\040order\040to\040efficiently\040perform\040calculations\040like\040field\040quantization\040in\040nonlocal\040domains\040which\040would\040be\040very\040difficult\040to\040perform\040otherwise\056)
/Keywords (16\040Jan\0402021\054\040Classical\040electromagnetism\054\040Electromagnetism\054\040Special\040relativity\054\040Quantization\040\050physics\051)
